@slow
Feature: Network exposure of the student-management host (DevSecOps Phase 2 - Acceptance)
  Only the application port may be reachable from outside; the database must not be.

  Background:
    Given "nmap" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name     | value         |
      | hostname | 192.168.56.10 |

  Scenario: The application port is open
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -Pn -p 8089 <hostname>
      """
    Then the output should match /8089.tcp\s+open/

  Scenario: MySQL is not exposed outside the Kubernetes cluster
    When I launch an "nmap" attack with:
      """
      nmap -Pn -p 3306,33060 <hostname>
      """
    Then the output should not match /3306.tcp\s+open/
    And the output should not match /33060.tcp\s+open/
